{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"In My Lap: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja67'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 67 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Itthivagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Women </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>7. Ucchaṅgajātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>In My Lap: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Ucchaṅge deva me putto, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>A son in my lap, Your Majesty, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Pathe dhāvantiyā pati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>or a husband while walking the street—</span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tañca desaṁ na passāmi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>but I don’t see the place </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yato sodariyamānayeti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>from where I can fetch a brother. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Ucchaṅgajātakaṁ sattamaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
